katoa K-8, Senmurv I-12\n• Zeruhn Mines: Koschei J-9, Kupala I-9, Radegast I-11' } } },
    { name = 'Elite Hunts', group = 'Server', desc = 'Scythe\'s 25 elite encounters, which unlock only after all 475 regular hunt NMs are dead, with the tier order and spawn rules for each. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/elite-hunts.html', steps = { { title = 'Unlock requirement', note = '• Your own character must kill all 475 regular hunt NMs first, and there is no way around this.\n• Until then the Hunts Master refuses you and no elite spawns.\n• Check progress with !huntstatus.' }, { title = 'Overview', note = '• The system has 24 field elites plus a final battlefield boss, 25 in total.\n• Clear the tiers in strict order: Seals (Tier 4), Champions (Tier 3), Specials (Tier 2), Supremes (Tier 1), Absolute Virtue.\n• Each elite also has its own conditions, such as Vana\'diel day, weather, moon phase, titles or zone kill counters.\n• Elites are level 99 with 15x HP/MP and 5x combat stats.\n• Each kill pays 250 Scyld, 10x the regular rate.\n• Elites are tuned for 6-player parties, though strong solo setups can handle some Seals.\n• \'Seal\' and \'Gyve\' mean the same thing: the 8 elemental Tier 4 bosses.\n• One Vana\'diel day lasts about 58 real minutes, and the week has 8 days (Firesday to Darksday).\n• The moon cycle lasts 84 days, so check /clock.\n• Some spawns depend on the Reive (Adoulin outdoor battle) state in a zone.' }, { title = 'Getting started', note = '• Confirm that you are eligible with !huntstatus.\n• Once eligible, the NM Hunts Master (Celennia Memorial Library) offers a new Elite board option.\n• Begin with a Tier 4 Seal; many players open with the Fire Seal (Cape Teriggan).\n• Go to the Seal\'s zone, kill the matching elementals to fill the counter, then wait for the listed weather.\n• Work up through the tiers using the prerequisites below.' }, { title = 'Tier 4 — Elemental Seals (Entry Point)', note = '• Fire Seal: Cape Teriggan (H-7). Kill 10 Fire Elementals, then wait for Hot Spell or Heat Wave.\n• Ice Seal: Fei\'Yin (H-6). Kill 10 Ice Elementals, then wait for Snow or Blizzards at night.\n• Wind Seal: Mamook (I-8). Kill 10 Air Elementals, then wait for Wind or Gales.\n• Earth Seal: Halvung (L-7). Kill 10 Earth Elementals, then wait for Dust Storm or Sand Storm on Earthsday.\n• Thunder Seal: Sacrarium (J-8). Kill 10 Thunder Elementals, then wait for thunder weather.\n• Water Seal: Crawlers\' Nest (E-8). Kill 10 Water Elementals, then wait for Rain or Squall with the moon at 80% or more.\n• Light Seal: Upper Delkfutt\'s Tower (J-10). Kill 10 Light Elementals, then wait for Auroras or Stellar Glare in daytime.\n• Dark Seal: Castle Zvahl Keep [S] (I-7). Kill 10 Dark Elementals, then wait for Gloom or Darkness in deep night.' }, { title = 'Tier 3 — Humanoid Champions', note = '• Each Champion needs at least one specific Seal cleared, plus its own conditions.\n• Perih Vashai: Abyssea-Tahrongi (H-10). Must be a solo player on Windsday.\n• Excenmille: Jugner Forest (I-8). San d\'Oria must control the region, on Lightsday.\n• Tenzen: Abyssea-Konschtat (E-9). Needs the Thunder Seal, Lightsday at dawn (5-7am), the Tenzen\'s Ally title and 25 Empty kills in the zone.\n• Prishe: Misareaux Coast (L-12). Needs the Ice Seal, a Half Moon and Cursed Soup active.\n• Robel-Akbel: Castle Oztroja [S] (H-11). Needs the Dark Seal, a New Moon, night and Darksday.\n• Iroha: Escha-Zi\'Tah (E-11). Needs the Wind Seal, Tenzen cleared, a Full Moon and dusk.' }, { title = 'Tier 2 — Special Bosses', note = '• Balamor: Foret de Hennetiel (F-5). Needs the Earth Seal and Robel-Akbel. All 10 Broadleaf Palms must be alive, with the reives untouched.\n• Kamlanaut: Ru\'Aun Gardens (J-9). Needs the Light Seal and Prishe. Kill 25 Light Elementals in the zone.' }, { title = 'Tier 1 — Supreme Beings', note = '• Hades: Caedarva Mire (I-10). All 6 ToAU kings in the zone must be dead.\n• Promathia: Grand Palace of Hu\'Xzoi. Needs Hades cleared, 100 kills in the zone and a Full Moon.\n• Metus: Kamihr Drifts (G-8). Needs Balamor and Hades. Every reive palisade in the zone must be dead.\n• Shinryu: Escha-Ru\'Aun (E-7). Needs Iroha and Metus, and the player must have nothing equipped.\n• Prov. Watcher: Abyssea-Misareaux (D-6). Needs all 8 Seals and 4 dragon titles.\n• Cl. of Darkness: Castle Zvahl Baileys [S] (F-6). Needs Robel-Akbel, the Dark Seal, the Medal of Altana, Darksday and night.\n• Hades Ascended: Reisenjima (G-9). Needs the Water Seal and Kamlanaut. Kill 30 Poroggos, but a Toad death resets the counter.' }, { title = 'Final — Absolute Virtue', note = '• After every field elite is cleared, Absolute Virtue appears in Mount Kamihr only when you request it from the Hunts Master.\n• AV cycles through all job abilities, each on a rotating cooldown.\n• Killing AV wipes all elite progress, so you start again from the Seals.' }, { title = 'BCNM — Time Devourer', note = '• Time Devourer is a battlefield fought with NPC assistance, not a field spawn.\n• It is separate from the field elite chain.' } } },
    { name = 'Gear and weapons', group = 'Server', desc = 'How Scythe changed relic stats and weapon skills, the ways to get Relic, Mythic, Empyrean and Aeonic (REMA) weapons, and how Fay weapon augments work. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/relic-weapons.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/weapon-progression.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/fay-weapons.html', steps = { { title = 'REMA Custom Mods', note = '• REMA means Relic, Empyrean, Mythic and Aeonic weapons.\n• All 14 relics have custom stats at the 75, 119 and 119-III tiers.\n• Mythic, Empyrean and Aeonic weapons follow their retail upgrade paths.\n• Relic weapon skills have OCC 35%/3x: a 35% chance to deal triple damage. Mandau\'s chance is 40%.\n• With multi-hit fTP replication, every hit of a multi-hit relic weapon skill uses the full fTP. On retail only the first hit does.' }, { title = 'Weapon Stats (119-III)', note = '• Spharai (MNK), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, DEX+30, ATT+70, ACC+50, STP+15, Haste+5%, DA+5%, Kick+20, Counter+14, MagDmg+186.\n• Mandau (THF), OCC 40%/3x: DEX+30, AGI+30, ATT+60, ACC+50, STP+15, TA+5%, Crit+5%, CritDmg+5, MagDmg+186.\n• Excalibur (PLD), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, VIT+30, ATT+60, ACC+50, STP+15, DA+8%, MagDmg+186.\n• Ragnarok (DRK), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, ATT+50, ACC+60, STP+15, DA+5%, Crit+15%, CritDmg+5, MagDmg+186.\n• Guttler (BST), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, CHR+30, ATT+60, ACC+50, STP+15, DA+8%, MagDmg+186.\n• Bravura (WAR), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, VIT+30, ATT+50, ACC+60, STP+15, DA+8%, MagDmg+186.\n• Apocalypse (DRK), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, INT+30, ATT+50, ACC+60, STP+15, Haste+5%, DA+5%, MagDmg+186.\n• Gungnir (DRG), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, ATT+50, ACC+60, STP+15, DA+8%, MagDmg+186.\n• Kikoku (NIN), OCC 35%/3x: DEX+30, AGI+30, ATT+60, ACC+50, STP+15, TA+5%, DW+5, MagDmg+186.\n• Amanomurakumo (SAM), OCC 35%/3x: STR+30, ATT+50, ACC+60, STP+20, Haste+5%, Zanshin+10, MagDmg+186.\n• Mjollnir (WHM), OCC 35%/3x: MND+35, VIT+30, ATT+40, ACC+40, STP+10, Haste+5%, Refresh+4, Cure Potency+25, MagDmg+248.\n• Claustrum (BLM/SMN), OCC 35%/3x: INT+40, MND+40, ACC+50, MAB+45, MACC+50, MagDmg+341.\n• Yoichinoyumi (SAM/RNG): RATT+45, RACC+60.\n• Annihilator (RNG): RATT+45, RACC+60, MagDmg+155.\n• The Database Equipment tab lists the custom stats at the 75 and 119 tiers.' }, { title = 'Relic Weaponskills', note = '• Relic weapon skills unlock by weapon skill level, so you can use them without the relic equipped.\n• Every relic weapon skill has fTP 5.0 / 9.0 / 13.0.\n• Single hit, no multi-hit fTP: Final Heaven (H2H) and Tachi: Kaiten (Great Katana).\n• Single hit, with multi-hit fTP: Mercy Stroke (Dagger), Knights of Round (Sword), Scourge (Great Sword), Onslaught (Club), Metatron Torment (Axe), Catastrophe (Scythe), Geirskogul (Polearm), Blade: Metsu (Katana), Randgrith (Club, WHM) and Gate of Tartarus (Staff).\n• Two hits, with full fTP on both: Namas Arrow (Archery) and Coronach (Marksmanship).' }, { title = 'Mythic / Empyrean / Aeonic changes', note = '• Mythic aftermath triggers on weapon skills, and its tiered buffs depend on the TP spent. Look up the stats in the Database Equipment tab with the Modifier filter.\n• Empyrean aftermath triggers on weapon skills on Scythe, not only on melee rounds as on retail. Empyrean weapon skills keep their retail fTP and hit counts.\n• Aeonic weapons use retail stats. Their aftermath gives Lv.1/2/3 based on TP spent, and their weapon skills use multi-hit fTP replication.' }, { title = 'Ways to get a weapon', note = '• !rema shop: once you pass the gate, buy a base Relic 75, Mythic 75 or Empyrean 80 for your current job at 5M gil each.\n• Traditional routes: Dynamis for Relic, Nyzul Isle, Einherjar and Assault for Mythic, Abyssea and Magian Trials for Empyrean, and Escha for Aeonic.\n• Hunt Kupons: Kupon I-RME at 400 unique NM kills and Kupon W-RMEA at 500.\n• Prime weapons are still a work in progress and have no released route.' }, { title = 'The 10 Gate HNMs', note = '• Kill each of these once, in any order, solo or in a group. Custom hunt NMs do not count.\n• King Behemoth: Behemoth\'s Dominion.\n• Aspidochelone: Valley of Sorrows.\n• Tiamat: Attohwa Chasm.\n• Medusa: Arrapago Reef.\n• Cerberus: Mount Zhayolm.\n• Khimaira: Caedarva Mire.\n• Hydra: Wajaom Woodlands.\n• Gurfurlur the Menacing: Halvung.\n• Gulool Ja Ja: Mamook.\n• Jormungand: Uleguerand Range.' }, { title = 'What\'s in the Shop', note = '• The shop only lists weapons for your current main job, so change jobs first to see other sets. Every weapon costs 5,000,000 gil.\n• WAR: Bravura, Ragnarok, Guttler, Conqueror, Ukonvasara, Farsha.\n• MNK: Spharai, Glanzfaust, Verethragna.\n• WHM: Mjollnir, Yagrush, Gambanteinn.\n• BLM: Claustrum, Laevateinn, Hvergelmir.\n• RDM: Murgleis, Almace.\n• THF: Mandau, Vajra, Twashtar.\n• PLD: Excalibur, Burtgang, Almace.\n• DRK: Apocalypse, Ragnarok, Liberator, Caladbolg, Redemption.\n• BST: Guttler, Aymur, Farsha.\n• BRD: Carnwenhan.\n• RNG: Yoichinoyumi, Annihilator, Gastraphetes, Gandiva.\n• SAM: Amanomurakumo, Kogarasumaru, Masamune.\n• NIN: Kikoku, Nagi, Kannagi.\n• DRG: Gungnir, Ryunohige, Rhongomiant.\n• SMN: Claustrum, Nirvana, Gambanteinn.\n• BLU: Tizona.\n• COR: Annihilator, Death Penalty, Armageddon.\n• PUP: Kenkonken.\n• DNC: Terpsichore, Twashtar.\n• SCH: Tupsimati.\n• GEO: Idris (Ergon, level 99).\n• RUN: Epeolatry (Ergon, level 99).\n• After buying, upgrade the usual way. The GEO and RUN Ergon weapons are already level 99 and use retail Bayld and job-point progression.' }, { title = 'Relic Weapons', note = '• Stage 1: get the base weapon from Dynamis currency and NM drops.\n• Stage 2 to 3: Ancient currency exchange with a 2-hour wait.\n• Stage 3 to 4: Ancient currency exchange with a 1-hour wait.\n• Stage 4 to 119: Riftcinder and Pluton.\n• 119 to 119-II: 300 Pluton in total.\n• 119-II to 119-III: 3,000 Pluton in total.\n• Scythe lowers the currency exchange rates and wait times.\n• Oboro & Forge Cache (Port Jeuno): store Pluton, Beitetsu, Riftborn, Riftcinder and Astral Detritus with the Forge Cache NPC, then trade your 99 AG weapon to Oboro.\n• Stage 1 there uses 300 stored materials. Stage 2 through 119-III needs 10,000 materials plus Scintillating Rhapsody.\n• Astral Detritus pays for RP augmentation.\n• The 14 relics are Spharai, Mandau, Excalibur, Ragnarok, Guttler, Bravura, Gungnir, Apocalypse, Kikoku, Amanomurakumo, Mjollnir, Claustrum, Yoichinoyumi and Annihilator.' }, { title = 'Mythic Weapons', note = '• Get the base weapon from Nyzul Isle Investigation (floor 100).\n• Upgrade it with Alexandrite plus Einherjar and Assault points.\n• Use Riftborn Boulder for 119, and 3,000 in total for 119-II to 119-III.\n• On Scythe, Alexandrite costs 25 Scyld each in the milestone shop.\n• Nyzul Isle casket drops and Vigil weapon drops are enabled.' }, { title = 'Empyrean Weapons', note = '• Start from a Magian Trial base weapon and complete the trials.\n• Use Beitetsu for 119, and 3,000 in total for 119-II to 119-III.\n• Scythe lowers the Magian kill counts and adjusts the conditions.\n• Beitetsu is sold in the Scyld milestone shop.' }, { title = 'Aeonic Weapons', note = '• Get the Sacred Kindred\'s Crest in Escha - Zi\'Tah.\n• Defeat Escha NMs for the key items.\n• Trade the key items and the crest for the Aeonic weapon.\n• You can also get one with Kupon W-RMEA at 500 unique hunt kills.' }, { title = 'The Hunt Shortcut', note = '• 400 unique kills: Kupon I-RME and 3,500 Scyld, which gives an RME weapon upgrade item.\n• 500 unique kills: Kupon W-RMEA and 7,500 Scyld, which gives any RMEA weapon you choose at 119-III.\n• 500 kills means every regular hunt NM (475), the 24 field elites and the final battlefield boss.' }, { title = 'Fay weapons', note = '• There are 20 eligible weapons, one per job. Callisto\'s dialogue lists them all.\n• Each of the 14 Shadowreign [S] zones has its own augment pool, so choose your zone based on the weapon.\n• Each reroll gives 1 or 2 augments with values inside set ranges.\n• Each weapon gets up to 5 rerolls before its augments are locked.\n• On a level 99 job, most Pixie NMs can be soloed with Trusts.' } } },
    { name = 'Lumina gear augments', group = 'Server', desc = 'Angel in Chocobo Circuit puts exact augment values on gear using auction house items charged with Faded Crystals. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/lumina-augments.html', steps = { { title = 'Checking augments', note = '• Each augment family is tied to an existing auction house item that cannot be equipped.\n• !lumina or !lumina all adds up the Lumina stat augments and auras on everything you have equipped.\n• !lumina slot main, or !lumina main, checks a single slot.\n• Auras that the client tooltip does not show are listed separately.\n• Duplicate aura types do not stack, so the command reports only the strongest one.' }, { title = 'Step 1: Charge the AH Item', note = '• Trade Angel one assigned auction house item plus Faded Crystals.\n• The number of crystals sets the exact power. For example, canteen_of_drachenfall_water with 4 Faded Crystals becomes a charged Attack +4 item.\n• Luminas are spent at this step.\n• Power 1-5 costs 30 Luminas.\n• Power 6-10 costs 75 Luminas.\n• Power 11-20 costs 150 Luminas.\n• Power 21-32 costs 300 Luminas.\n• Higher special paths cost 600 Luminas.' }, { title = 'Step 2: Apply It to Gear', note = '• Trade Angel the charged item plus one weapon or armor piece. She uses up the item and hands back the gear with the augment on it.\n• Every stat augment fills the next free slot, even when the same family is already on the gear.\n• Repeated stat augments stack, so compare your total against the server limit.\n• Auras reuse the gear\'s single aura slot.' }, { title = 'Aura Augments', note = '• Aura gear gives a GEO-style effect to nearby allies while you wear it.\n• Use the single plate_of_indi-* items from the Geomancy auction house category.\n• Different aura types work together, but for the same type only the strongest one applies.\n• Regen: plate_of_indi-regen gives party Regen.\n• Refresh: plate_of_indi-refresh gives party Refresh.\n• Haste: plate_of_indi-haste gives party magic haste.\n• Fury: plate_of_indi-fury gives party attack and ranged attack.\n• Precision: plate_of_indi-precision gives party accuracy and ranged accuracy.\n• Focus: plate_of_indi-focus gives party magic accuracy.\n• Barrier: plate_of_indi-barrier gives party defense percent.\n• Fend: plate_of_indi-fend gives party magic defense.\n• Acumen: plate_of_indi-acumen gives party magic attack.' }, { title = 'How to Identify Tokens', note = '• Trade Angel an assigned item on its own and she tells you what it controls.\n• For a charged item, she tells you the stored augment or aura power.' } } },
    { name = 'Endgame activities', group = 'Server', desc = 'How Scythe runs server-wide Siege raids, 60-minute Sortie runs and Dynamis Divergence zones. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/siege.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/sortie.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/dynamis-divergence.html', steps = { { title = 'Siege: How to join', note = '• A Siege is a server-wide raid of 5 waves. It is currently the main live source of Exemplar Points (EP) for Master Levels.\n• When a siege starts, every online player gets a linkshell-chat notice and an on-screen callout naming the zone.\n• Travel with !headto to the nearest city, or use your home point or a Warp spell. The zone stays open while the event runs.\n• Join any party or fight solo. EP is tracked for each player, and Trusts are scaled up for sieges.\n• Waves 1-3 form the approach, wave 4 is a gauntlet, and the boss arrives in wave 5.\n• When it ends, EP is paid by contribution, with a minimum for anyone who stayed to the finish.' }, { title = 'Siege: Bosses', note = '• Each boss phase changes its ability rotation and enrage timer.\n• Bosses take reduced damage except during called-out vulnerability windows.\n• Siege bosses use siege-only mechanics such as telegraphed AoEs, mobile stacks and role-tagged debuffs.\n• On-screen callouts announce every major mechanic, and no addon is needed.\n• Cover, Rampart, Palisade, Sentinel, Majesty and similar abilities gain special effects during siege mechanics.' }, { title = 'Siege: Rewards', note = '• EP scales with participation.\n• The final boss drops phase-gated loot.\n• Your first clear unlocks a completion title.' }, { title = 'Sortie: Overview', note = '• Sortie is a 60-minute instance in Outer Ra\'Kaznar [U1] with sectors A-H.\n• Every sector has a roaming minor NM. Major NMs unlock through sector gadgets.\n• Aminon is the final boss and needs the basement fragment chain.\n• Rewards are Gallimaufry, temporary progression items, Ra\'Kaz. Sapphires and Ra\'Kaz. Starstones.\n• Ruspix in Leafallia uses these for Empyrean armor +2 and +3 upgrades.' }, { title = 'Sortie: Steps', note = '• Get a Shiny Ra\'Kaznarian plate from Ruspix in Leafallia.\n• At Frontier Bivouac #4 in Kamihr Drifts, use the Diaphanous Transposer.\n• Enter the instance. Your plate turns dull when the run starts.\n• Clear sectors and collect shards, sheets, fragments and metals.\n• After the run, spend your Gallimaufry with Ruspix.' }, { title = 'Sortie: Sectors', note = '• A: minor NM Abject Obdella, major NM Ghatjot (Ra\'Kaz. Sapphire). Items: Key, Plate, Sheet, Shard, Metal A.\n• B: minor NM Biune Porxie, major NM Leshonn (Sapphire). Items: Key, Plate, Sheet, Shard, Metal B.\n• C: minor NM Cachaemic Bhoot, major NM Skomora (Sapphire). Items: Key, Plate, Sheet, Shard, Metal C.\n• D: minor NM Demisang Deleterious, major NM Degei (Sapphire). Items: Key, Plate, Sheet, Shard, Metal D.\n• E: minor NM Esurient Botulus, major NM Dhartok (Ra\'Kaz. Starstone). Items: Shard E, Fragment 1, Metal E.\n• F: minor NM Fetid Ixion, major NM Gartell (Starstone). Items: Shard F, Fragment 2, Metal F.\n• G: minor NM Gyvewrapped Naraka, major NM Triboulex (Starstone). Items: Shard G, Fragment 3, Metal G.\n• H: minor NM Haughty Tulittia, major NM Aita (Starstone). Items: Shard H, Fragment 4, Metal H.\n• Final: Aminon (Starstone), which needs the basement fragment chain.' }, { title = 'Sortie: Rewards', note = '• Minor NMs give 195-480 Gallimaufry, depending on the sector.\n• Major NMs A-D give 2,000 Gallimaufry and a chance at a Sapphire.\n• Major NMs E-H give 10,000 Gallimaufry and a chance at a Starstone.\n• Aminon gives 30,000 Gallimaufry and a Starstone.\n• Chests, caskets, coffers and aurums give 100-3,000 Gallimaufry plus sector items.\n• Ruspix +2 costs an Empyrean +1 piece, 1 Ra\'Kaz. Sapphire and 10,000 Gallimaufry.\n• Ruspix +3 costs an Empyrean +2 piece, 1 Ra\'Kaz. Starstone and 70,000 Gallimaufry.' }, { title = 'Divergence: Available Zones', note = '• Dynamis-Bastok [D]: alliance of 12-18. Drops Galka/Hume relic armor, currency and Ambuscade-equivalent items.\n• Dynamis-San d\'Oria [D]: alliance of 12-18. Drops Elvaan relic armor, currency and upgrade items.\n• Dynamis-Windurst [D]: alliance of 12-18. Drops Tarutaru/Mithra relic armor, currency and upgrade items.\n• Dynamis-Jeuno [D]: full party of 6. Drops Alexandrite, rare currency variants and unique Jeuno pieces.' }, { title = 'Divergence: Notes', note = '• Unlike original Dynamis, the [D] zones have a distinct set of enemies and bosses, with different mechanics and drops.\n• Each zone has Disjoined beastman mini-bosses with unique mechanics: Disjoineds_Galka, Disjoineds_Elvaan, Disjoineds_Mithra and Disjoineds_Tarutaru.\n• Elemental Circle mobs, such as Fire Circle and Ice Circle, drop crafting and upgrade materials.\n• Disjoineds_Odin is the final boss of Jeuno Divergence and drops the top-tier currency variant.\n• The [D] zones use the standard Divergence drop tables.' } } },
    { name = 'FATE', group = 'Server', desc = 'Scythe\'s timed open-world events: how to join, how scoring and Lumina/EXP rewards work, and the FATE list for each zone with level cap and map grid. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/fate.html', steps = { { title = 'Overview', note = '• A FATE is a timed event in your current zone: either a swarm of enemies or one strong boss inside a marked area.\n• Anyone in the zone can join, everyone shares rewards, and each player is scored separately.\n• 88 FATEs in 44 outdoor zones spanning the 1-99 leveling path, plus Abyssea, Adoulin and Escha zones.\n• Zone level caps run 12-99; players above the cap are synced down.\n• Spawn check: each in-game hour, with at most one active FATE per zone.\n• Cooldown after completion: annihilation 40 min, notorious 60-120 min.\n• Event radius: 55-85 yalms from center, depending on the FATE.\n• Currency: Luminas (charvar [FATE]Luminas).\n• A Gold finish gives up to 20% of your next level in EXP.\n• Solo is possible; a party is advised for the Abyssea/Escha bands.' }, { title = 'How to join', note = '• Go to a FATE-enabled zone; a FATE may spawn when the in-game hour changes, if its cooldown has expired.\n• Watch zone chat for the [FATE] message, which gives the event name, landmark/map grid and time limit.\n• Go to the landmark and talk to the FATE Sync NPC at the center of the circle to get level-synced.\n• Engage: FATE mobs cannot be targeted until a synced player engages, then they become active for everyone.\n• Fight inside the radius (default 60 yalms); both kills and time inside count toward your score.\n• When the FATE ends, rewards are handed out automatically by individual score; no looting or party required.' }, { title = 'Contribution & Rewards', note = '• Score = kill credit (10 per trash mob, 120 per notorious boss) + 1 point per second inside the radius.\n• Pet and trust kills credit their owner; the killer\'s whole party is added; players on the enmity list also get credit.\n• Gold: score 120+, 10 Luminas, EXP = 20% of next level.\n• Silver: score 40-119, 4 Luminas, EXP = 8%.\n• Bronze: score 1-39, 1 Lumina, EXP = 2%.\n• The EXP percentage uses the EXP needed at the zone\'s level cap: Gold at a level-85 Abyssea FATE is about 9,800 raw EXP, at a level-99 Adoulin FATE about 11,200.\n• Scythe\'s map.EXP_RATE multiplier (4x) is applied after that.' }, { title = 'FATE Types', note = '• The announcement does not state the type: many enemies means annihilation, one large mob means notorious.\n• Annihilation: 15-min timer; kill 10-24 mobs depending on level band; a second wave arrives once the first is about half cleared and raises the target; mobs have 3x HP and 2x attack/defense.\n• Notorious: one boss using its family\'s native mob skills, beat it before time runs out; tuned for a party at the cap, solo needs gear and job advantage.\n• Notorious (low): 20-25 min, 10x HP, 5x stats.\n• Notorious (mid): 30 min, 12x HP, 6x stats.\n• Notorious (high): 35-40 min, 15x HP, 7-8x stats.' }, { title = 'Zone Roster — Starter (Lv 12-30)', note = '• Key: A = Annihilation, N = Notorious. Solo-friendly with trusts.\n• East Sarutabaruta (cap 12): Sarutabaruta Bloom Frenzy A H-11; Sarutabaruta Crawler Queen N J-9.\n• North Gustaberg (cap 12): Goblin Raiding Party A L-7; Ancient Rock Eater N D-10.\n• South Gustaberg (cap 12): South Gustaberg Skirmish A E-9.\n• West Ronfaure (cap 12): Hound Pack Assault A H-8; Alpha Hound Uprising N H-9.\n• West Sarutabaruta (cap 12): Sarutabaruta Procession A J-8; Sarutabaruta Raptor Tyrant N H-11.\n• Konschtat Highlands (cap 15): Highland Horror Swarm A H-6; Konschtat Ancient N E-9.\n• La Theine Plateau (cap 15): Orc Warband Advance A H-11; Plateau Hare Stampede A H-9; Plateau Overlord N E-7.\n• Tahrongi Canyon (cap 15): Tahrongi Canyon Swarm A I-8.\n• Buburimu Peninsula (cap 25): Buburimu Dhalmel Stampede A H-9; Buburimu Sky Wyrm N I-7.\n• Valkurm Dunes (cap 25): Shore Fiend Surge A G-8; Dune Horror Awakened N L-6.\n• Jugner Forest (cap 30): Jugner Forest Horde A I-8.\n• Meriphataud Mountains (cap 30): Meriphataud Beetle Swarm A E-6; Meriphataud Raptor Surge A E-11 (listed as needing repair); Axe Beak Ascendant N E-6.\n• Pashhow Marshlands (cap 30): Pashhow Marsh Swarm A K-6; Quadav Marsh Patrol A I-7; Marsh Goobbue Rising N E-11; Pashhow Malboro Bloom N I-10.\n• Qufim Island (cap 30): Qufim Weapon Surge A H-7.' }, { title = 'Zone Roster — Midgame (Lv 35-65)', note = '• Sauromugue Champaign (cap 35): Champaign Beast Rush A F-6; Champaign Yagudo Rally A K-8; Champaign Coeurl Stalker N J-7; Sauromugue Tyrant N K-10.\n• Batallia Downs (cap 40): Undead Legion Rising A K-9; Barrow Wight Lord N F-8.\n• Bibiki Bay (cap 40): Bibiki Bay Shore Swarm A H-6.\n• Lufaise Meadows (cap 40): Lufaise Bugard Charge A K-9.\n• Rolanberry Fields (cap 40): Rolanberry War Party A J-6; Rolanberry Ochu N I-13.\n• Beaucedine Glacier (cap 45): Glacier Gigas Reinforcements A H-10; Glacier Horde A G-7 (listed as needing repair); Glacier Stone Warden N H-9.\n• The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah (cap 45): Sanctuary Pilgrimage Surge A H-8; Zi\'Tah Stone Colossus N G-11.\n• Misareaux Coast (cap 55): Misareaux Shore Surge A K-11; Orcish Coast Raid A K-7; Misareaux Goaftrap Bloom N G-7.\n• Xarcabard (cap 55): Shadow Tide A H-8; Xarcabard Shadow Drake N I-9.\n• Western Altepa Desert (cap 60): Altepa Scorpion March A H-10; Antican War Party A I-5; Desert Ancient N K-7.\n• Cape Teriggan (cap 65): Teriggan Raptor Hunt A G-8; Cape Manticore Tyrant N I-9.\n• Uleguerand Range (cap 65): Uleguerand Snowpack A G-11.' }, { title = 'Zone Roster — Veteran (Lv 75-85)', note = '• Meriphataud Mountains [S] (cap 75): Meriphataud Lynx Ambush A E-5.\n• Newton Movalpolos (cap 75): Newton Moblin Works A F-10; Newton Bugbear Watchman N F-10.\n• Ru\'Aun Gardens (cap 75): Ru\'Aun Elemental Surge A H-11; Ru\'Aun Despot Awakens N J-8.\n• Valley of Sorrows (cap 75): Valley Raptor Rampage A J-8; Valley Sea Terror N G-8.\n• Beadeaux [S] (cap 80): Beadeaux Quadav Vanguard A F-7.\n• Abyssea-Attohwa (cap 85): Toxic Horror Eruption A L-9; Attohwa Rift Predator N J-8.\n• Abyssea-La Theine (cap 85): Abyssean Beast Surge A J-8; Abyssal Geier N I-8.\n• Abyssea-Tahrongi (cap 85): Twisted Nightmare Swarm A H-7; Canyon Abyssite Titan N G-5.\n• Escha Ru\'Aun (cap 85): Ru\'Aun Predator Surge A I-10; Escha Ru\'Aun Sovereign N G-10.' }, { title = 'Zone Roster — Endgame (Lv 90-99)', note = '• Escha Zi\'Tah (cap 90): Escha Legion Surge A H-8; Escha Zi\'Tah Entity N J-10.\n• West Sarutabaruta [S] (cap 93): Saruta Rarab Migration A, western war fields; Saruta Rarab Matron N, eastern burrow.\n• Batallia Downs [S] (cap 95): Batallia Fly Swarm A, western downs; Batallia Tsetse Matron N, eastern nesting ground.\n• Rolanberry Fields [S] (cap 95): Rolanberry Crawler March A, northern berry fields; Rolanberry Crawler Regent N, southern crawler nest.\n• Sauromugue Champaign [S] (cap 95): Champaign Beetle Breakout A, western war ridge; Champaign Beetle Bulwark N, eastern carapace field.\n• Ceizak Battlegrounds (cap 99): Ceizak Beastmen Siege A J-10; Ceizak Warlord N H-10.\n• Grauberg [S] (cap 99): Grauberg Sapling Surge A, western sapling grove; Grauberg Sapling Elder N, southern sapling grove.\n• Kamihr Drifts (cap 99): Kamihr Beast Horde A H-9; Kamihr Sovereign N J-7.\n• Yorcia Weald (cap 99): Weald Beast Rampage A J-11; Weald Ancient Treant N G-9.' }, { title = 'Tips', note = '• Talk to the Sync NPC before attacking; attacking unsynced makes the mob reset and disengage.\n• If a trust engages before you have synced, the mobs can stay locked, so sync yourself first.\n• Time score is credited as 5 points every 5 seconds inside the circle; leaving stops new time credit but keeps what you earned.\n• BST charmed pets, SMN avatars and trust kills all count for you.\n• Cooldowns are tracked per FATE; zones such as Pashhow and Sauromugue rotate 4 FATEs, so a busy zone usually has one within 10-15 minutes.\n• Even Bronze pays 1 Lumina and a small EXP bonus.\n• Sync will not replace an existing LEVEL_RESTRICTION effect; the FATE message asks you to remove it first.' } } },
    { name = 'Abyssea custom pops', group = 'Server', desc = 'On Scythe, Abyssea NMs are popped by trading items to a ??? in the zone rather than by key-item chains; this lists each pop item and the scripted drops of the Boosted 125 versions. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/abyssea.html', steps = { { title = 'Abyssea Custom Pops', note = '• Abyssea is otherwise retail-based; trade the listed item(s) to the matching ??? in the zone to pop the NM, no key-item chain needed.\n• Boosted 125 entries are selected level-125 versions with stronger stats and bonus upgrade-item rewards.\n• Pops per zone: Altepa 20, Attohwa 23, Grauberg 20, Konschtat 21, La Theine 21, Misareaux 22, Tahrongi 21, Uleguerand 20, Vunkerl 22.\n• VNM entries give the approximate map square of the fixed ???; your <pos> may read an adjacent square if you stand near a border.\n• In the zone pop lists, \'+\' means trade all listed items together; \'Normal + Boosted\' means both versions use the same pop item.' }, { title = 'Boosted 125 Drop Table', note = '• Normal NMs keep the retail drop table; Boosted 125 versions drop the scripted rewards below instead.\n• Altepa: Bennu, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Balance (3223/3224/3222/3225); Dragua, 8x Dragua\'s Scale (3288); Rani, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Vision (3211/3212/3210/3213).\n• Attohwa: Itzpapalotl, 8x Itzpapalotl\'s Scale (2962); Smok, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Balance; Ulhuadshi, 8x Ulhuadshi\'s Fang (2963).\n• Grauberg: Alfard, 8x Alfard\'s Fang (3291); Azdaja, 8x Azdaja\'s Horn (3292); Raja, 8x Iron Plate (3293).\n• Konschtat: Bloodeye Vileberry, 2x Jewel of Vision (3212), 4x Card of Vision (3213) and 2x Coin of Vision (3211); Eccentric Eve, 8x Spool of Malboro Fiber (837); Kukulkan, 4x Kukulkan\'s Fang (2932) and 4x Kukulkan\'s Skin (2497).\n• La Theine: Briareus, 8x Helm of Briareus (2929); Carabosse, 8x Carabosse\'s Gem (2930); Hadhayosh, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Wieldance (3219/3220/3218/3221).\n• Misareaux: Amhuluk, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Ardor (3215/3216/3214/3217); Cirein-croin, 8x Cirein-croin\'s Lantern (2965); Sobek, 8x Sobek\'s Skin (2964).\n• Tahrongi: Chloris, 8x Two-leaf Chloris Bud (2928); Glavoid, 8x Glavoid Shell (2927); Lacovie, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Ardor.\n• Uleguerand: Apademak, 8x Apademak\'s Horn (3289); Isgebind, 8x Isgebind\'s Heart (3290); Pantokrator, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Voyage (3227/3228/3226/3229).\n• Vunkerl: Bukhis, 8x Bukhis\'s Wing (2966); Durinn, 2x each Coin/Jewel/Stone/Card of Wieldance; Sedna, 8x Sedna\'s Tusk (2967).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Altepa', note = '• Amarok: Sharabha Hide (3231) + Tiger Kings Hide (3232) + High-quality Dhalmel Hide (3238).\n• Bennu: Chocobo Feather (840), Normal + Boosted.\n• Brulo, VNM ??? G-8: Fire Cluster (4104).\n• Bugul Noz: Handful of Sabulous Clay (3243).\n• Chickcharney: High-quality Cockatrice Skin (3240).\n• Dragua: Vial of Dragon Blood (1133), Normal + Boosted.\n• Emperor de Altepa: Bottle of Oasis Water (3234) + Sprig of Giant Mistletoe (3244).\n• Fire Elemental or Earth Elemental, VNM ??? L-5: Faded Crystal (613).\n• Ironclad Smiter: Vial of Tablilla Mercury (3230) + Smoldering Arm (3236).\n• Koios, VNM ??? J-9 near J-8 border: Earth Cluster (4107).\n• Orthus: Cerberus Claw (2168).\n• Rani: Golem Shard (955), Normal + Boosted.\n• Sharabha: Sand-caked Fang (3237).\n• Shaula: Vial of Vadleany Fluid (3233) + High-quality Scorpion Claw (3242).\n• Tablilla: Sandy Shard (3235).\n• Vadleany: Ladybird Leaf (3241).\n• Waugyl: Vial of Puppets Blood (3239).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Attohwa', note = '• At\'euvhi, VNM ??? I-10 near H-10 border: Clump of Bee Pollen (9082).\n• Berstuk: Extended Eyestalk (3080).\n• Blazing Eruca: Eruca Egg (3073).\n• Drekavac: Set of Wailing Rags (3077).\n• Es\'euvhi, VNM ??? J-9: Lump of Beeswax (913).\n• Gaizkin: Vial of Undying Ooze (3075).\n• Granite Borer: Withered Cocoon (3072).\n• Itzpapalotl: Bat Wing (922), Normal + Boosted.\n• Kampe: Gory Pincer (3079).\n• Kharon: Handful of Bone Chips (3076).\n• Lusca, VNM ??? J-8 near K-8 border: Sack of Little Worm Mulch (1831).\n• Maahes: Coeurl Round (3081).\n• Mielikki: Great Root (3084).\n• Nightshade: Withered Bud (3082).\n• Pallid Percy: Vial of Undying Ooze (3075).\n• Smok: Handful of Dragon Scales (867), Normal + Boosted.\n• Svarbhanu: Cracked Dragonscale (3078).\n• Titlacauan: Demon Horn (902).\n• Ulhuadshi: Hecteyes Eye (939), Normal + Boosted.\n• Wherwetrice: Mangled Cockatrice Skin (3083).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Grauberg', note = '• Air Elemental, VNM ??? E-12 near F-12 border: Faded Crystal (613).\n• Alfard: Hydra Fang (2158), Normal + Boosted.\n• Amphitrite: Coral Fragment (887).\n• Azdaja: Wyvern Skull (905), Normal + Boosted.\n• Bomblix Flamefinger: Jar of Goblin Gunpowder (3264) + Jar of Goblin Oil (3274).\n• Burstrox Powderpate: Length of Goblin Rope (3273).\n• Gamayun, VNM ??? K-12: Wind Cluster (4106).\n• Ika-Roa: High-quality Pugil Scale (3270).\n• Ironclad Sunderer: Teekesselchen Fragment (3260) + Darkflame Arm (3266).\n• Lorelei: Fay Teardrop (3271).\n• Maere, VNM ??? J-8 near J-9 border: Dark Cluster (4111).\n• Minaruja: Pursuers Wing (3267).\n• Ningishzida: Minaruja Skull (3261) + Jaculus Wing (3262) + High-quality Wivre Hide (3268).\n• Raja: Cermet Chunk (931), Normal + Boosted.\n• Teekesselchen: Flask of Bubbling Oil (3265).\n• Teugghia: Naiads Lock (3263) + Unseelie Eye (3272).\n• Xibalba: Decaying Molar (3269).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Konschtat', note = '• Alkonost: Giant Bugard Tusk (2912).\n• Arimaspi: Clouded Lens (2913).\n• Ashtaerh the Gallvexed: Murmuring Globule (2914).\n• Bloodeye Vileberry: Normal uses Vial of Beastman Blood (930); Boosted uses Bottle of Avatar Blood (1626).\n• Bloodguzzler: Vial of Eft Blood (2903).\n• Bombadeel: Clump of Snakeskin Moss (2909).\n• Clingy Clare: Tiny Morbol Vine (2907).\n• Depths Digester, VNM ??? K-11: Hope Crystal (4075).\n• Eccentric Eve: Normal uses Malboro Vine (920); Boosted uses Ameretat Vine (2361).\n• Fear Gorta: Square of Moonglow Cloth (2905).\n• Hadal Satiator, VNM ??? L-7: Fulfillment Crystal (4076).\n• Hexenpilz: Oblivispore Mushroom (2908).\n• Keratyrannos: Armored Dragonhorn (2910).\n• Kukulkan: Normal uses Peiste Skin (2523); Boosted uses Peiste Stinger (2524).\n• Lentor: Giant Slug Eyestalk (2904).\n• Meanderer, VNM ??? G-13: Thought Crystal (4074).\n• Sarcophilus: Ripped Eft Skin (2911).\n• Siranpa-Kamuy: Rotting Eyeball (2906).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-La Theine', note = '• Adamastor: Trophy Shield (2894).\n• Baba Yaga: Piceous Scale (2898).\n• Briareus: Gigas Necklace (499), Normal + Boosted.\n• Brooder, VNM ??? D-8 near D-9 border: Remnant of a Bitter Memory (1607).\n• Carabosse: Phoenix Feather (844), Normal + Boosted.\n• Dozing Dorian: Dried Chigoe (2891).\n• Grandgousier: Massive Armband (2896).\n• Hadhayosh: Ram Horn (895), Normal + Boosted.\n• La Theine Liege: Transparent Insect Wing (2897).\n• Lugarhoo: Filthy Gnole Claw (2902).\n• Meditator, VNM ??? C-6: Remnant of a Burning Memory (1606).\n• Megantereon: Gargantuan Black Tiger Fang (2893).\n• Nguruvilu: Winter Puk Egg (2899).\n• Pantagruel: Oversized Sock (2895).\n• Poroggo Dom Juan: Bug-eaten Hat (2900).\n• Ruminator, VNM ??? F-9: Remnant of a Radiant Memory (1612).\n• Toppling Tuber: Giant Agaricus Mushroom (2901).\n• Trudging Thomas: Raw Mutton Chop (2892).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Misareaux', note = '• Amhuluk: Yagudo Feather (841), Normal + Boosted.\n• Avalerion: Bird Feather (847).\n• Cep-Kamuy: Chunk of Orobon Meat (5563).\n• Cirein-croin: Handful of Fish Scales (864), Normal + Boosted.\n• Funereal Apkallu: Apkallu Feather (2149).\n• Ironclad Observer: Chunk of Iron Ore (643).\n• Ironclad Pulverizer: Iron Ingot (651).\n• Karkatakam: Crab Shell (881).\n• Manohra: Giant Bird Feather (842).\n• Mighrah, VNM ??? J-8: Cluster Core (1667).\n• Minax Bugard: Bugard Tusk (1622).\n• Mxghrah, VNM ??? F-5 near G-5 border: Infinity Core (1474).\n• Nehebkau: Raptor Skin (853).\n• Nonno: Two-leaf Mandragora Bud (4368).\n• Npfundlwa: Rabbit Hide (856).\n• Sirrush: Wyvern Skin (1122).\n• Sobek: Handful of Dragon Scales (867), Normal + Boosted.\n• Tristitia, VNM ??? F-4: Baitball (4004).\n• Tuskertrap: Flytrap Leaf (1617).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Tahrongi', note = '• Abas: Eft Egg (2922).\n• Alectryon: Chunk of Cockatrice Tailmeat (2923) + Quivering Eft Egg (2949).\n• Cannered Noz: Baleful Skull (2918).\n• Chloris: Normal uses Dryad Root (923); Boosted uses Snow Lily (1725).\n• Gancanagh: Clump of Alkaline Humus (2920).\n• Glavoid: Normal uses Gnat Wing (2522); Boosted uses Antlion Jaw (1616).\n• Halimede: High-quality Clionid Wing (2915).\n• Hedetet: Venomous Scorpion Stinger (2921) + Clump of Acidic Humus (2948).\n• Hungerer, VNM ??? F-11: Remnant of a Fleeting Memory (1608).\n• Lachrymater: Moaning Vestige (2926).\n• Lacovie: Normal uses Adamantoise Shell (908); Boosted uses Treant Bulb (953).\n• Muscaliet: Resilient Mane (2925) + Smooth Whisker (2950).\n• Ophanim: Shriveled Wing (2945) + Tarnished Pincer (2946) + Bloodshot Hecteye (2917).\n• Tefenet: Shocking Whisker (2924).\n• Treble Noctules: Bloody Fang (2919) + Exorcised Skull (2947).\n• Usurper, VNM ??? H-8: Remnant of a Somber Memory (1611).\n• Vetehinen: High-quality Limule Pincer (2916).\n• Yearner, VNM ??? J-8 near J-9 border: Remnant of a Profane Memory (1609).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Uleguerand', note = '• Anemic Aloysius: Sandworm Fang (2515).\n• Apademak: Khimaira Tail (2373), Normal + Boosted.\n• Audumbla: Buffalo Horn (1615).\n• Blanga: Gargouille Horn (2747).\n• Chillwing Hwitti: Imp Horn (2157).\n• Chione, VNM ??? G-10: Ice Cluster (4105).\n• Dhorme Khimaira: Khimaira Tail (2373).\n• Ice Elemental or Water Elemental, VNM ??? G-10: Faded Crystal (613).\n• Ironclad Triturator: Iron Ingot (651).\n• Isgebind: Dragon Heart (4486), Normal + Boosted.\n• Koghatu: Golem Shard (955).\n• Ogopogo, VNM ??? H-8: Water Cluster (4109).\n• Pantokrator: Orichalcum Gearbox (9145), Normal + Boosted.\n• Resheph: Ball of Cyclone Cotton (4045).\n• Upas-Kamuy: Chunk of Ice Ore (1256).\n• Veri Selen: Wyvern Wing (1124).\n• Yaguarogui: Black Tiger Fang (884).' }, { title = 'Abyssea-Vunkerl', note = '• Armillaria: Puffball (4448).\n• Bukhis: Buffalo Horn (1615), Normal + Boosted.\n• Chhir Batti: Pinch of Bomb Ash (928).\n• Durinn: Giant Femur (893), Normal + Boosted.\n• Dvalinn: Bone Chip (880).\n• Gnawtooth Gary: Wild Onion (4387).\n• Hm\'zdei, VNM ??? G-4: Artificial Lens (1109).\n• Iku-Turso: Coral Fragment (887).\n• Kadraeth the Hatespawn: Soulflayer Tentacle (2335).\n• Karkadann: Unicorn Horn (1841).\n• Ketea, VNM ??? J-12: Chunk of Super Cermet (1772).\n• Khalkotaur: Bronze Ingot (649).\n• Pascerpot: Magic Pot Shard (954).\n• Quasimodo: Gargouille Horn (2747).\n• Rakshas: Black Tiger Fang (884).\n• Sedna: Ruszor Fang (2754), Normal + Boosted.\n• Seps: Pinch of Venom Dust (944).\n• Vu\'zdei, VNM ??? D-10 near D-11 border: Chunk of Orpiment (2126).\n• Xan: Lizard Tail (926).' } } },
    { name = 'Regional bosses', group = 'Server', desc = 'Scythe has 40 open-world regional bosses; each can be brought forward by completing a rite in its ritual zone. Timers are live and not included here. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/regional-bosses.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/data/regional_bosses.json', steps = { { title = 'How rites work', note = '• Each boss still has its normal respawn timer.\n• Finishing the rite only moves the already-scheduled spawn earlier; it does not reroll it or reveal the hidden lair.\n• Rite progress counts only inside the listed ritual zone.\n• "Straight" below means continuous time.' }, { title = 'Original regions', note = '• Super Briarhorn (Ronfaure): West Ronfaure; Thorn Tithe = 8 player deaths.\n• Super Dunetide (Zulkheim): Valkurm Dunes; Dune Banquet = 90 food-minutes pooled across living players.\n• Super Ironroot (Norvallen): Jugner Forest; Council of Roots = 6 living players on 6 distinct main jobs, 3 min straight.\n• Super Slagwurm (Gustaberg): North Gustaberg; Forge the Vein = 60 kills finished by weapon skill.\n• Super Miremother (Derfland): Pashhow Marshlands; Broodpool Harvest = 40 kills during rain or squalls.\n• Super Starsting (Sarutabaruta): West Sarutabaruta; Hive Alarm = /panic, /point, /slap, /cheer, 3 times with no error.\n• Super Galeplume (Kolshushu): Buburimu Peninsula; Gale Run = 10,000 yalms combined movement while alive.\n• Super Razortalon (Aragoneu): Meriphataud Mountains; Predator\'s Vigil = 6+ living players in combat, 3 min straight.\n• Super Frostmaul (Fauregandi): Beaucedine Glacier; Whiteout Vigil = 6 living players resting together in snow/blizzard, 3 min straight.\n• Super Dreadwing (Valdeaunia): Xarcabard; Dread Toll = 12 player deaths at Vana\'diel night (18:00-05:59).\n• Super Deepwrath (Qufim): Qufim Island; Drain the Tide = 6 living players at 10% MP or less, 2 min straight.\n• Super Stoneheart (Li\'Telor): The Sanctuary of Zi\'Tah; Stone Stillness = 8 living players resting with nobody in the zone engaged, 3 min straight.\n• Super Imperator (Kuzotz): Eastern Altepa Desert; Three Banners = 9 living players from San d\'Oria, Bastok and Windurst, 3 min straight.\n• Super Ashmane (Vollbow): Cape Teriggan; Trial by Flame = 40 kills on Firesday.\n• Super Vinequeen (Elshimo Lowlands): Yuhtunga Jungle; Feed the Canopy = 6 fooded players on 6 distinct main jobs, 3 min straight.\n• Super Grudge (Elshimo Uplands): Yhoator Jungle; Silent Resentment = 6 living Silenced players together, 30 sec straight.\n• Super Skysunder (Tu\'Lia): Ru\'Aun Gardens; Three Nations Salute = one /salute from a citizen of each of San d\'Oria, Bastok, Windurst.\n• Super Ironfist (Movalpolos): Oldton Movalpolos; Iron Fists = 50 kills finished by MNK or PUP.\n• Super Doomhoof (Tavnazian Archipelago): Lufaise Meadows; Last Breath = 6 living players at 25% HP or less, 2 min straight.\n• Super Voidmind (Promyvion): Promyvion-Holla; Empty the Memory = 6 living players at 5% MP or less with no food, 2 min straight.\n• Super Luminarch (Lumoria): Al\'Taieu; Prismatic Assembly = Hume, Elvaan, Tarutaru, Mithra and Galka present, 3 min straight.' }, { title = 'Aht Urhgan', note = '• Super Dreadtusk (West Aht Urhgan): Bhaflau Thickets; Tasting Table = 8 living players with 8 different food effects, 2 min straight.\n• Super Scalejaw (Mamool Ja Savagelands): Wajaom Woodlands; Warband Challenge = WAR /angry, MNK /psych, THF /grin, WHM /praise, BLM /fume, RDM /salute.\n• Super Ashwing (Halvung): Mount Zhayolm; Firewalk = 8,000 yalms combined at 50% HP or less in hot spell/heat wave.\n• Super Mindreaver (Arrapago): Arrapago Reef; Mourner\'s Wake = DRK /kneel, WHM /cry, BLM /think, BRD /fume (Curse not needed).\n• Super Gearstorm (Alzadaal): Alzadaal Undersea Ruins; Clockwork Call = /point, /salute, /clap, /cheer in order twice with no error; no Vana-hour wait.' }, { title = '[S] fronts', note = '• Super Warbringer (Ronfaure Front): East Ronfaure [S]; Last Stand = 6 living players at 25% HP or less across 3+ main jobs, 2 min straight.\n• Super Moonfang (Norvallen Front): Jugner Forest [S]; Moonlit Hunt = 50 kills at night with the moon 50%+.\n• Super Cragscale (Gustaberg Front): North Gustaberg [S]; Hold the Quarry = 75 kills where the killer is in a party of 6+.\n• Super Bogstare (Derfland Front): Vunkerl Inlet [S]; Plague March = 8,000 yalms combined while alive and Poisoned.\n• Super Rotbloom (Sarutabaruta Front): West Sarutabaruta [S]; Garden of Rot = 6 Poisoned players with 6 different food effects, 2 min straight.\n• Super Stormlynx (Aragoneu Front): Meriphataud Mountains [S]; Storm Drill = 40 weapon-skill kills in wind, gales, thunder or thunderstorms.\n• Super Icebreaker (Fauregandi Front): Beaucedine Glacier [S]; Warm the Line = 8 fooded players resting together in snow/blizzard, 3 min straight.\n• Super Grimstone (Valdeaunia Front): Xarcabard [S]; Four Funeral Orders = deaths in order tank (PLD/RUN/WAR), healer (WHM/SCH), mage (BLM/RDM/GEO), scout (THF/NIN/DNC), done twice.' }, { title = 'Abyssea, Adoulin, Escha, Reisenjima', note = '• Super Abyssmaw (Abyssea): Abyssea-La Theine; Blood Constellation = 8 living Visitants at 20% HP or less, 90 sec straight; a player dying in the zone resets it.\n• Super Gutterfang (Adoulin Islands): Rala Waterways; Five Peoples Procession = a /wave from each of Hume, Elvaan, Tarutaru, Mithra, Galka.\n• Super Magmashell (East Ulbuka): Yahse Hunting Grounds; Three Shells = 9 players for 2 min straight: 3 at 1-33% HP, 3 at 34-66% HP and 3 at 67-100% HP.\n• Super Riftmaw (Escha Zi\'Tah): Escha Zi\'Tah; Rift Hunt = 6 local NM kills.\n• Super Starshroud (Escha Ru\'Aun): Escha Ru\'Aun; Twelve-Star Crown = /kneel from 12 different main jobs.\n• Super Voidreaver (Reisenjima): Reisenjima; Paradox Cycle = in order: 1 player death, 30 food-minutes, 20 weapon-skill kills, then /point, /kneel, /cheer, /panic.' } } },
    { name = 'Trusts and Login Points', group = 'Server', desc = 'Trust facts, upgrade currency and tiers on Scythe, plus the Login Point campaign and its prize list. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/trusts.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/login-points.html', steps = { { title = 'Trust basics', note = '• Trusts are summoned NPC party members; up to 5 at once, for a 6-member party including you.\n• Each has a fixed job and role; some have II versions that are stronger or behave differently.\n• Scythe has 122 trusts, obtained from story missions, nation quests, Records of Eminence, or bought with Login Points from the Greeter Moogle.' }, { title = 'Upgrade currency', note = '• Trust Stone (Tier I) = 5 Merit Points.\n• Trust Gem (Tier II) = 10 Merit Points or 100 Job Points.\n• Trust Jewel (Tier III) = 500 Job Points.\n• These are character variables, not items; exchange at the Trust Stone Exchange NPC in Ru\'Lude Gardens.' }, { title = 'How to upgrade a trust', note = '• All 122 trusts have 3 tiers; each tier costs stones, gems or jewels plus a specific trade item, sometimes with a nation rank, job level, fame, crafting skill or kill-count gate.\n• About half have explicit per-tier effects (new spells, stat scaling, job abilities); the rest benefit from generic systems such as the tank enmity siphon and tiered stat multipliers.\n• Convert Merit/Job Points to currency in Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n• Find the trust\'s upgrade NPC, which uses that trust\'s model, in the starting nations, Jeuno, Adoulin or a few special zones (e.g. Zeid in Bastok Mines, Shantotto in Windurst Walls, Maat in Ru\'Lude Gardens).\n• Talk to the NPC to see that tier\'s requirements.\n• Trade the item; it and the currency are consumed, the tier goes up, and it applies on your next summon.' }, { title = 'Login Points', note = '• The 365-day Login Campaign started April 11, 2026.\n• 500 points for the first login each day; 100 for each extra login that day.\n• Up to 1,500 points carry into the next month; no monthly reset during the campaign.\n• Spend at the Greeter Moogle in South San d\'Oria, Bastok Markets or Windurst Woods.' }, { title = '10 Points', note = '• Beastmen\'s Seal, Kindred\'s Seal, Kindred\'s Crest, High Kindred\'s Crest, Sacred Kindred\'s Crest.' }, { title = '100 Points — Set 1', note = '• Ciphers: Zeid, Lion, Naja Salaheem, Lehko Habhoka, Luzaf, Najelith, D. Shantotto, Star Sibyl, Karaha-Baruha, Areuhat.\n• Mog Kupon I-S1; Eudaemon Blade, Cape, Ring, Sash, Shield; Drill Calamary and Dwarf Pugil (fishing bait); Astral Cube (furnishing).' }, { title = '100 Points — Set 2', note = '• Ciphers: Uka Totlihn, Kuyin Hathdenna, Abenzio, Rughadjeen, Lhe Lhangavo, Mayakov, Brygid, Mildaurion, Rongelouts, Robel-Akbel, Ullegore, Teodor, Darrcuiln.\n• Excalipoor (weapon); Piece of Copse Candy (food).' }, { title = '100 Points — Set 3', note = '• Ciphers: Shantotto II, Ovjang, Mnejing, Sakura, Aldo, A Moogle, Fablinix, Elivira, Noillurie, Lhu Mhakaracca, Ferreous Coffin, Mumor.\n• Goobbue, Crab and Beetle Mounts; Cumulus Masque (head); Blizzard Brand (weapon).' }, { title = '100 Points — Set 4', note = '• Ciphers: Cid, Rahal, Koru-Moru, Babban, Gilgamesh, Qultada, Adelheid, Amchuchu, Semih Lafihna, Halver, Rainemard, Margret, Kukki-Chebukki.\n• Dhalmel Mount.' }, { title = '100 Points — Set 5', note = '• Ciphers: Lion II, Zeid II, Tenzen II, Prishe II, Nashmeira II, Lilisette II, Ingrid II, August, Rosulatia, Mumor II, Kupofried, Leonoyne, Maximilian, Kayeel-Payeel, Abquhbah, Makki-Chebukki, King of Hearts, Morimar, Monberaux.' }, { title = '500 Points', note = '• Facility Ring (EXP bonus); Caliber Ring (CP bonus).\n• Instrument quest items: Copy of Melodious Plans, Timbre Case Kit, Musichinery Kit.\n• Jug pet food: Jug of Honey Wine, Beastly Shank, Clump of Blue Pondweed.' }, { title = '1,000 Points', note = '• Jug pet food: Cup of Sweet Tea, Savory Shank, Clump of Red Pondweed.' } } },
    { name = 'Trust roster', group = 'Server', desc = 'Per-Trust summary: job, role, origin, how to get it, and what each upgrade tier costs. Every tier costs the same currency (T1 5 Trust Stones, T2 10 Trust Gems, T3 5 Trust Jewels) plus the listed trade item [item ID]; login-point Trusts all cost 100 points. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/trusts.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/trusts/<name>.html (one page per Trust)', steps = { { title = 'Ark Angel EV', note = '• WHM (no sub), Healer, RoZ; Unlocked via Zilart story content.\n• T1 Valor Coronet [15078] (PLD AF head); T2 Sulevia\'s Mask [25659] (Ambuscade head); T3 Burtgang 119 [20649] (Mythic weapon).' }, { title = 'Ark Angel GK', note = '• SAM/DRG, Melee DD, RoZ; Unlocked via Zilart story content.\n• T1 Myochin (SAM AF) legs [14225]; T2 Flamma Dirs [25873] (Ambuscade legs); T3 Gungnir 119 [20925] (Relic Polearm).' }, { title = 'Ark Angel HM', note = '• PLD/WAR, Tank / Melee DD, RoZ; Unlocked via Zilart story content.\n• T1 Hachiya Hatsuburi [27675] (NIN AF Reforged head); T2 Hizamaru Somen [25663] (Ambuscade head); T3 Usukane Haramaki [14554] (Salvage body).' }, { title = 'Ark Angel MR', note = '• BLM/RDM, Magic DD, RoZ; Unlocked via Zilart story content.\n• T1 Beast Helm [12517] (BST AF head); T2 Meghanada Visor [25661] (Ambuscade head); T3 Aymur 119 [20792] (Mythic Axe) + BST Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Ark Angel TT', note = '• RNG/NIN, Ranged DD, RoZ; Unlocked via Zilart story content.\n• T1 Chaos Flanchard [14221] (DRK AF legs); T2 Jhakri Pigaches [25933] (Ambuscade feet); T3 Apocalypse 119 [20880] (Relic Scythe) + DRK Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Abenzio', note = '• Goobbue (unique creature) (no sub), Melee DD (creature), SoA; login points set 2.\n• T1 Temple Gaiters [14090] (MNK AF feet); T2 Mummu Kecks [25875] (Ambuscade legs); T3 Tali\'ah Turban [25590] (Ambuscade head).' }, { title = 'Abquhbah', note = '• WAR (no sub), Melee DD, SoA; login points set 5.\n• T1 Valor Breeches [15123] (PLD AF legs); T2 Flamma Gambieras [25940] (Ambuscade feet); T3 Spharai 75 [18264] (MNK Relic weapon).' }, { title = 'Adelheid', note = '• SCH (no sub), Flexible Healer / Magic DD, SoA; login points set 4.\n• T1 Argute Gown [11307] (SCH Empyrean body) + SCH Lv50+; T2 Mallquis Chapeau [25583] (Ambuscade head); T3 Akademos [21150] (SCH Aeonic weapon) + SCH Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Ajido-Marujido', note = '• BLM (no sub), Nuker (magic DD), Windurst (base); Windurst Trust quest.\n• T1 Wizard\'s Gloves [13964] (BLM AF hands) + Windurst Rank 4; T2 Jhakri Cuffs [25808] (Ambuscade hands); T3 Claustrum 119 [21135] (Mythic Staff) + Windurst Rank 10.' }, { title = 'Aldo', note = '• THF (no sub), Melee DD, RoZ/Jeuno; login points set 3.\n• Upgrade at base Aldo in Port Jeuno; he wants Meghanada Gloves then Aeneas. Aldo (UC) is a different NPC with other requirements.\n• T1 Rogue\'s Armlets [13966] (THF AF hands) + any job Lv30+; T2 Meghanada Gloves [25802] (Ambuscade hands); T3 Aeneas [20594] (Aeonic Dagger) + THF Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Aldo (UC)', note = '• THF/WAR, Melee DD, Jeuno; Unity Concord: join a Unity, then talk to a Unity NPC.\n• Upgrade at Aldo (UC) in Upper Jeuno. If the NPC asks for Meghanada Gloves or Aeneas, that is base Aldo (Port Jeuno) instead.\n• T1 Rogue\'s Culottes [14219] (THF AF legs) + Norg fame Lv5; T2 Meghanada Chausses [25860] (Ambuscade legs); T3 Naegling [21621] (Ambuscade Sword) + THF Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Amchuchu', note = '• RUN/WAR, Magic Tank, SoA; login points set 4.\n• T1 Futhark Coat [26842] (RUN AF body) + RUN Lv99+; T2 Meghanada Cuirie [25747] (Ambuscade body); T3 Erilaz Galea [26782] (RUN Empyrean head).' }, { title = 'Apururu (UC)', note = '• WHM (no sub), Healer, Windurst; Unity Concord: join a Unity, then talk to a Unity NPC.\n• Base kit: Cure up to V, Curaga (also used on Sleep), all -na spells, Erase, Protectra, Shellra, Haste on melee, Stoneskin on self, Convert when MP < 25%.\n• Tier effects: T1 Cure Potency +15 and Regen I/II (cast on party under 90% HP); T2 Cure Potency 30 total, Regen III, Haste II; T3 Cure Potency 50 total, Regen IV, Raise (used on KO\'d members).\n• T1 Cleric\'s Bliaut [15089] (WHM AF body) + Windurst Rank 3; T2 Inyanga Jubbah [25751] (Ambuscade body); T3 Yagrush 119 [21062] (Mythic weapon) + WAR Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Arciela', note = '• RDM / BLM (no sub), Magic Hybrid, SoA; Finish the SoA missions; an Arciela II version exists.\n• T1 Duelist\'s Boots [15136] (RDM AF feet); T2 Jhakri Pigaches [25933] (Ambuscade feet); T3 Morrigan\'s Pigaches [15727] (Salvage feet).' }, { title = 'Arciela II', note = '• RDM / BLM (no sub), Magic Hybrid, SoA; Upgraded form of Arciela, through SoA missions.\n• T1 Duelist\'s Tabard [15091] (RDM AF body); T2 Jhakri Slops [25867] (Ambuscade legs); T3 Hadean Abjuration: Body [2435] (Einherjar).' }, { title = 'Areuhat', note = '• DRK (no sub), Melee DD (Pure Offense), San d\'Oria; login points set 1.\n• T1 Valor Surcoat [15093] (PLD AF body); T2 Flamma Korazin [25779] (Ambuscade body); T3 Wyrmal Abjuration: Body [1335] (Einherjar).' }, { title = 'August', note = '• PLD (no sub), Tank, SoA; login points set 5.\n• Base: 50% DT, Enmity +25, Fast Cast +20, HP +10%, full PLD abilities and spells, Daybreak under 66% HP (3 min recast), enmity siphon.\n• Tier effects: T1 Shield Block +20%; T2 block 40% total and Daybreak recast 2 min; T3 block 100% of blockable hits, adds Raise, and Daybreak also heals the party 15% of max HP.\n• T1 Valor Surcoat [15093] (PLD AF body); T2 Sulevia\'s Platemail [25745] (Ambuscade body); T3 Excalibur 119 [20645] (Relic weapon).' }, { title = 'Ayame', note = '• SAM (no sub), Melee DD, Bastok (base); Bastok Trust quest.\n• T1 Myochin (SAM AF) body [13781] + Bastok Rank 3; T2 Hizamaru Haramaki [25749] (Ambuscade body); T3 Amanomurakumo 119 [21015] (Relic GKT) + SAM Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Ayame (UC)', note = '• SAM/WAR, Melee DD, Bastok; Unity Concord: join a Unity, then talk to a Unity NPC.\n• T1 Myochin (SAM AF) head [13868] + Bastok Rank 5; T2 Hizamaru Somen [25663] (Ambuscade head); T3 Kogarasumaru 119 [21017] (Mythic GKT) + SAM Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Babban', note = '• Mandragora (unique creature) (no sub), Melee DD (creature), SoA; login points set 4.\n• T1 Temple Hose [14215] (MNK AF legs); T2 Mummu Wrists [25820] (Ambuscade hands); T3 Tali\'ah Seraweels [25871] (Ambuscade legs).' }, { title = 'Balamor', note = '• DRK (no sub), Melee DD, SoA; Finish the SoA missions.\n• T1 Chaos Flanchard [14221] (DRK AF legs); T2 Sulevia\'s Gauntlets [25800] (Ambuscade hands); T3 Liberator 119 [20882] (Mythic Scythe).' }, { title = 'Brygid', note = '• NPC (unique) (no sub), NPC (minimal combat), SoA; login points set 2.\n• Buffs the master: base CHR +5 / Defense +20; T1 CHR 8 / Def 40; T2 CHR 10 / Def 60; T3 CHR 12 / Def 80 (totals).\n• T1 Astral Ring [13548] + any job Lv50+; T2 Jhakri Coronal [25667] (Ambuscade head) + GEO Lv50+; T3 Idris [21070] (GEO Mythic) + GEO Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Chacharoon', note = '• THF (no sub), Melee DD, SoA; Finish the SoA missions.\n• T1 Rogue\'s Culottes [14219] (THF AF legs) + any job Lv30+; T2 Mummu Kecks [25875] (Ambuscade legs); T3 Morrigan\'s Robe [14562] (Salvage body) + THF Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Cherukiki', note = '• WHM (no sub), Healer, Windurst (base); Windurst Trust quest.\n• T1 Cleric\'s Pantaloons [15119] (WHM AF legs) + Windurst Rank 2; T2 Inyanga Shalwar [25865] (Ambuscade legs) + WAR Lv60+; T3 Piety Duckbills [27332] (WHM Relic feet) + WAR Lv99+.' }, { title = 'Cid', note = '• SCH in Light Arts mode (no sub), Healer, Bastok (base); login points set 4.\n• T1 5x Cermet Chunk [931] + Bastok Rank 3; T2 3x Darksteel Sheet [664] + Bastok Rank 6; T3 Annihilator 119 [21260] + Bastok Rank 10.' }, { title = 'Cornelia', note = '• Geomancer-style aura support (no sub), Support / Buffer (Passive), General; Special event.\n• Base: Indi-Haste aura plus Accuracy, Ranged Accuracy and Magic Accuracy +20 on the master; these become +30 (T1), +40 (T2), +50 (T3).\n• T1 Cleric\'s Duckbills [15134] (WH