re, 151 MP, 5.5s/8s)\n• Thunder Breath: Wyvern (Thunder, 193 MP, 7.0s/48s)\n• Triumphant Roar: Gargouille (Fire, 36 MP, 1.75s/26s)\n• Uppercut: Goobbue (Physical, 31 MP, 0.5s/18s)\n• Vanity Dive: Wanderer (Physical, 58 MP, 0.5s/42s)\n• Vapor Spray: Phuabo (Water, 172 MP, 3.0s/19s)\n• Venom Shell: Uragnite (Water, 86 MP, 3.0s/45s)\n• Vertical Cleave: Euvhi (Physical, 86 MP, 0.5s/37s)\n• Voracious Trunk: Marid / IrizIma (Wind, 72 MP, 10.0s/56s)\n• Warm-Up: Mamool Ja (Physical, 59 MP, 3.0s/56s)\n• Water Bomb: Poroggo (Water, 67 MP, 2.5s/32s)\n• Whirl of Rage: Evil Weapon (Physical, 73 MP, 1.0s/31s)\n• White Wind: Puk (Wind, 145 MP, 7.0s/20s)\n• Wild Carrot: Rabbit (Physical, 37 MP, 2.5s/6s)\n• Wild Oats: Mandragora (Physical, 9 MP, 0.5s/7s)\n• Wind Breath: Dragon (Wind, 26 MP, 1.0s/30s)\n• Winds of Promy: Thinker (Omen) (Light, 36 MP, 2.5s/18s)\n• Yawn: Apkallu (Light, 55 MP, 3.0s/60s)\n• Zephyr Mantle: Puk (Wind, 31 MP, 4.0s/60s)\n• Blastbomb: Orc (Fire, 36 MP, 2.25s/15s)\n• O. Counterstance: Warlord Orc (Fire, 18 MP, 4.0s/11s)\n• Nature\'s Meditation: Chapuli (Fire, 38 MP, 1.0s/60s)\n• Tempestuous Upheaval: Twitherym (Wind, 133 MP, 0.5s/12s)\n• Rending Deluge: Cracklaw (Water, 118 MP, 2.0s/35s)\n• Embalming Earth: Matamata (Earth, 57 MP, 3.0s/24s)\n• Paralyzing Triad: Umbril (Physical, 33 MP, 0.5s/15s)\n• Foul Waters: Acuex (Water, 76 MP, 3.5s/60s)\n• Glutinous Dart: Velkk (Physical, 16 MP, 0.5s/6s)\n• Retinal Glare: Panopt (Light, 26 MP, 0.5s/45s)\n• Subduction: Marolith (Wind, 27 MP, 1.0s/5s)\n• Erratic Flutter: Wamoura (Wind, 92 MP, 2.0s/45s)\n• Restoral: Gear (Light, 127 MP, 2.0s/10s)\n• Rail Cannon: Gear (Light, 200 MP, 2.5s/180s)\n• Diffusion Ray: Chariot (Light, 238 MP, 4.0s/45s)\n• Sinker Drill: Wulgaru (Physical, 91 MP, 0.5s/20s)\n• Molting Plumage: Tulfaire (Wind, 146 MP, 1.0s/25s)\n• Nectarous Deluge: Snapweed (Water, 97 MP, 3.0s/45s)\n• Sweeping Gouge: Raaz / Calydontis (Physical, 29 MP, 0.5s/120s)\n• Atra Libations: Dullahan (Dark, 164 MP, 4.0s/180s)\n• Searing Tempest: Scorched Yanthu (Fire, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Spectral Floe: Glaciated Yanthu (Ice, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Anvil Lightning: Electrified Yanthu (Thunder, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Entomb: Entombed Yanthu (Earth, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Saurian Slide: Velkk (Physical, 109 MP, 0.5s/35s)\n• Palling Salvo: Fluturini (Dark, 175 MP, 3.0s/45s)\n• Blinding Fulgor: Scorched Yanthu (Light, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Scouring Spate: Glaciated Yanthu (Water, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Silent Storm: Electrified Yanthu (Wind, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Tenebral Crush: Entombed Yanthu (Dark, 116 MP, 6.0s/60s)\n• Uproot: Yumcax (Light, 88 MP, 1.5s/30s)\n• Crashing Thunder: Hurkan (Thunder, 172 MP, 1.0s/30s)\n• Polar Roar: Kumhau (Ice, 126 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Mighty Guard: Shinryu (Light, 299 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Cruel Joke: Dhokmak / Palloritus (Dark, 187 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Cesspool: Dhokmak / Rancibus (Water, 166 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Tearing Gust: Ashrakk / Putraxia (Wind, 202 MP, 3.0s/30s)' }, { title = 'Spells from Notorious Monsters', note = '• These 12 come only from specific NMs, all reachable on Scythe; learn them the same way.\n• Thrashing Assault: Mammet, Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (Physical, 119 MP, 0.5s/60s)\n• Thunderbolt: Behemoth / King Behemoth, Behemoth\'s Dominion (Thunder, 138 MP, 3.5s/30s)\n• Harden Shell: Adamantoise / King Adamantoise, Ru\'Aun Gardens (Earth, 20 MP, 1.5s/30s)\n• Absolute Terror: Ouryu / Wyrm, Riverne Site #B01 (Dark, 29 MP, 0.5s/30s)\n• Gates of Hades: Cerberus, several zones incl. Temenos (Fire, 156 MP, 3.5s/30s)\n• Tourbillion: Khimaira, Caedarva Mire (Physical, 108 MP, 1.0s/30s)\n• Pyric Bulwark: Hydra, Wajaom Woodlands (Light, 50 MP, 1.5s/30s)\n• Bilgestorm: Pandemonium Warden (Dvergr), Aydeewa Subterrane (Physical, 122 MP, 1.0s/30s)\n• Bloodrake: Vampyr / Nosferatu, various zones (Nosferatu in Caedarva Mire) (Physical, 99 MP, 0.5s/30s)\n• Droning Whirlwind: Colkhab (Bztavian NM), Bhaflau Thickets (Earth, 76 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Carcharian Verve: Rockfin, Arrapago Reef (Thunder, 52 MP, 3.0s/30s)\n• Blistering Roar: Gabbrath, Halvung (Light, 28 MP, 3.0s/30s)' } } },
    { name = 'Getting started', group = 'Server', desc = 'How to connect to Scythe, make an account and character, and what to do on first login. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/getting-started.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/server-info.html', steps = { { title = 'Connection', note = '• Server: ffxiscythe.duckdns.org (new public host; standard ports are used automatically).\n• Bootloader: Ashita v4 with LandSandBoat xiloader 1.1.5.\n• Boot argument: --server ffxiscythe.duckdns.org\n• Existing Ashita users: add a separate xiloader boot profile with that argument and launch it from Ashita.\n• Setup takes roughly 30 minutes.' }, { title = 'Install the FFXI client', note = '• Install the official FFXI client first, keeping PlayOnline Viewer and Common Files; no retail subscription is needed.\n• The launcher pins the chosen folder to Scythe\'s signed client version and can roll back newer retail files, so keep a separate copy if you also play retail.\n• Do not drop in replacement DAT files; the launcher checks and repairs the managed client itself.' }, { title = 'Scythe Launcher 3.0.39 (update pending)', note = '• 3.0.39 is the prior release and still targets the old server; editing its managed profile does not make Play Scythe work.\n• Until the revised launcher ships, play through the separate Ashita profile; if Ashita is not set up yet, wait for the new launcher.\n• SHA-256: 5080AC2A214754AF82A44726F1A9902CC1C712F9539D584682D2994DB72234D0\n• Windows requirements: .NET Framework 4.8+ and Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 Redistributable (x86); the launcher offers official downloads if missing.\n• It is not Authenticode-signed (may show Unknown publisher); check the hash and do not disable antivirus or add exclusions.\n• Close FFXI, PlayOnline Viewer, Ashita, Windower and xiloader.\n• Download the launcher and confirm the SHA-256.\n• Run it; if no client is found, use Choose FFXI Folder.\n• Click Check VPS Release, then Match Client to Scythe, and leave it open until verification finishes.\n• Connect with the separate Ashita profile for the new server.' }, { title = 'Create an account', note = '• In the xiloader console pick Create Account, set a username and password, then pick Login with them.\n• Up to two accounts per player may be online together for dual-boxing.\n• Lost passwords cannot be recovered automatically.\n• If your password may be exposed, use Change Password in xiloader before using the website; only enter it in xiloader or the official Scythe login page, never in Discord or chat.' }, { title = 'Create a character and play', note = '• Make a character and choose a starting nation; every map and a server linkpearl are granted on first login.\n• Type !buff to enable the levelling buff (scaling Regen/Refresh/Regain plus 200% EXP).\n• Type !cc to warp to Chocobo Circuit, the custom hub with auction house, crafting guild vendors, crystal moogle, Advanced Support NPC and mission-item shop.\n• Next, follow the site\'s Guides page ("Your First Hour" plus four progression paths: new player, returning vet, solo, endgame hunter); ask in Discord if stuck.' } } },
    { name = 'Rules and FAQ', group = 'Server', desc = 'Scythe\'s conduct rules, enforcement policy and answers to common questions. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/rules.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/faq.html', steps = { { title = 'Conduct', note = '• No harassment, hate speech, slurs or targeted abuse.\n• Real-money trading of items, currency or accounts means an immediate permanent ban.\n• No bots, speed hacks, packet manipulation or unfair exploits; report bugs instead.\n• Maximum two accounts per player, both allowed online at once.\n• Use English in /shout and /yell; private chat may be any language.' }, { title = 'Gameplay rules', note = '• Whoever engages an NM first holds claim.\n• No deliberate MPKs, training mobs onto others, or interfering with another fight.\n• Do not grief someone camping an NM spawn; take disputes to staff.\n• Report anything giving unintended rewards or content skips in Discord; abusing bugs is punished.' }, { title = 'Enforcement', note = '• First offenses usually get a warning.\n• Staff rulings are final; appeal privately via Discord DM to a staff member.\n• RMT and botting get immediate permanent bans with no warning.' }, { title = 'Cost and era', note = '• Free: you need the FFXI client (no subscription) and a free bootloader such as Ashita or Windower; no cash shop, donation perks or premium tier.\n• All expansions through Rhapsodies of Vana\'diel; level cap 99 plus Master Levels; not era-locked.\n• No wipes are planned; any forced partial reset would be announced in advance.' }, { title = 'NM hunts', note = '• 475 regular hunt NMs across 145 zones, plus 24 field elites and a final battlefield boss unlocked by full completion (500 encounters).\n• Regular hunt NMs are level 80 with doubled HP/MP and combat stats and respawn every 9–11 minutes.\n• Kills pay Scyld, spendable on rewards including Mog Kupons for gear and weapons.\n• At 99, warp to Eastern Adoulin and talk to Eppel-Treppel to enter the Celennia Memorial Library; the NM Hunts Master there handles daily/weekly bounties, the unique-kill tracker and the Elite board, with the NM Hunt shop NPC beside him.\n• Elite Hunts unlock only after unique kills of all 475 regular NMs (repeats do not count; no skipping).\n• Elite order: Seals → Champions → Specials → Supremes → Absolute Virtue.' }, { title = 'Weapons, solo and multibox', note = '• Relics are rebalanced (fTP 5.0/9.0/13.0, full multi-hit fTP replication, triple damage procs); mythic, empyrean and aeonic weapons follow standard upgrade paths.\n• Most of the 475 regular NMs can be soloed with preparation; Trusts are available.\n• The 25 elite hunts, Dynamis Divergence and Siege raids are tuned for groups.\n• Colosseum Solo mode: 0.5x boss HP, 2.5x EP reward.\n• Dual-boxing with two simultaneous accounts is allowed.' }, { title = 'Server features', note = '• Includes 25 gated elite encounters, a planned 5-tier Colosseum, 50 Master Levels, server-wide siege raids, Dynamis Divergence and Fay weapon augments.\n• 4× EXP, no death penalty and an equal subjob ratio.\n• Chocobo Circuit (!cc from anywhere): auction house, all 9 crafting guild material vendors (always open, no rank needed), crystal vendor, crystal storage moogle, and the Advanced Support NPC for the 15-minute Imagery craft buff.' }, { title = 'Exemplar Points', note = '• EP is the Master Level currency, tracked per job; each ML gives +1 all stats, +7 HP and +2 MP.\n• Current EP sources: siege participation and boosted Abyssea NMs; the Colosseum (in development) is planned as the top source.' }, { title = 'Bugs and legality', note = '• Report bugs in Discord #bug-reports with zone, what you did, what happened, what you expected, and screenshots if possible.\n• Scythe is a free fan project that distributes no Square Enix files and claims no ownership of FFXI; players use their own legitimately obtained clients.' } } },
    { name = 'Work in progress', group = 'Server', desc = 'Systems the site marks as still in development and not yet live when the page was fetched. Source: https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/coming-soon.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/server-info.html, https://scythe-bbq.pages.dev/features.html', steps = { { title = 'Unreleased content list', note = '• Original systems: The Hollow Crown and Colosseum, Ferry and Sky Pirates, Chocobo Raising, New Game Plus, Arcane Sigils.\n• Retail content not yet released: Delve, Omen, Odyssey, Vagary, Incursion, Sinister Reign, Walk of Echoes, Meeble Burrows, Moblin Maze Mongers, Legion, Einherjar/Odin, Salvage, High-Tier and Sacred Kindred Crest battlefields, A.M.A.N. Trove, Skirmish.\n• Ambuscade access and shop flow is also unfinished.\n• Code existing in the development tree does not mean a feature is released.' }, { title = 'The Hollow Crown & Colosseum', note = '• Original Lumina campaign with player choices, based on the eight Colosseum clearances.\n• Has five private encounters, world witnesses and three endings with equal rewards.\n• Still needs in-game route testing, multiplayer checks, balancing and release approval.' }, { title = 'Hollow Crown: requirements', note = '• Be a Job Master with 2,100 Job Points on your current job.' }, { title = 'Hollow Crown: Silver clearance', note = '• After the Blooding Match, equip a Reraise Hairpin and talk to Ysabet next to the Planar Rift in the Eldieme Necropolis.\n• Listen to her whole story.\n• Trade only the charged Ceremonial Dagger, 12 Bone Chips and 3 Revival Tree Roots.\n• The dagger is consumed and you receive a Dark Ring.' }, { title = 'Hollow Crown: tracking', note = '• Open The Hollow Crown menu at the Arena Master to see your current objective.' }, { title = 'Ferry & Sky Pirates', note = '• Pirate fights planned on sea routes; optional airship ambushes send you to a separate battlefield.\n• Routes, encounter flow, return trips and rewards are still being validated.' }, { title = 'Chocobo Raising', note = '• Raise your own chocobo from egg to adult through daily feeding, grooming and training.\n• Colour and stats depend on parentage and care.\n• Testable now but not complete.' }, { title = 'New Game Plus', note = '• Progression framework for max-level characters, currently disabled.\n• The NPC and reward design exist; the character-reset step is deliberately turned off.' } } },
}

return S
